## Ingest conventions

- If a PDF, slide deck, or similar source already has an extracted `.txt` file next to it, ingest from the extracted text first. Re-extract only if the source changed or the text is missing/outdated.
- If both preparation slides and meeting notes exist for the same event, read the slides first and then the meeting notes so the notes are interpreted in context.
- If a repeatedly used external or shared source folder has no durable ingest tracker yet, create and maintain an `INGESTED.md` file there. Use it to record what was ingested, duplicates, and the source of record.

